STUDENT’S NAME: PHUONG DAO
CODING PROJECT 2: Sampling and Reconstruction
EE-125
Professor: Jordan Rosenthal
Date submitted: 10/05/2026

Objective: This lab demonstrates the fundamental relationship between continuous-time and 
discrete-time signals. Sampling shows how continuous signals are converted into digital data, 
while undersampling demonstrates aliasing and the loss of signal information when the sampling 
rate is too low. Interpolation then shows how a continuous signal can be reconstructed from its samples. 
These concepts are essential in practical applications such as ADCs, sensors, audio, communications, and digital signal processing.
